<H3><CENTER><FONT COLOR="#ffff00"><A HREF="mailto:nareman@virk.co.uk">Nareman Virk</A></FONT></CENTER></H3>



        Nareman has a 1992 Fiat Tipo 2.0 16V, five door in Bianco
        white - not many of those around! It's now covered 97,000 miles.
        He has owned five Fiat Tipos since
        he passed his driving test in 1991 and he strongly believes that
        the Tipo 16V is the best hot hatch that you can buy. He has
        been approached by a complete stranger in a car park who offered
        to buy his car but Nareman says what would he replace it with?
        <P>
        Nareman has not had the best of luck with the car, one of it's
        spark plugs melted and fell into the engine. Needless to say,
        his engine was not happy and sounded like a tractor. Luckily, it
        happened near his house, so he managed to get home. It needed
        a new head and was in the garage for 2-3 weeks. To make things
        worse the bottom end of the engine had only been rebuilt about
        six months earlier and he had been without the car for almost
        two months. During this rebuild (65,000 miles) he had a
	new clutch, new brake pads and discs all round and a new radiator.
        <P>
        He has had his latest Sedicivalvole since 1996 and has made several
        modifications to it including removing the catalytic converter, a
        K&amp;N performance filter and a full Remus exhaust system. Removing
        the catalytic converter gives a dramatic improvement in mid-range
        performance. Nareman estimates his car now produces 160 bhp and
        0-60 mph acceleration has come down from 7.9 to 7.3 seconds.
        <P>
        Nareman believes, like the rest of us, that he is addicted to driving
        the car. He regularly takes it to 7000 rpm when warmed up and
        second gear acceleration through a tunnel is awesome - the noise
        with the windows down is...well, frightening!
        <P>
        Nareman has 15&quot; Momo Extreme wheels fitted to his car. He also
        has clear oval side repeaters and a 16V badge on the front grill
        off the Fiat Coupe. The car also has Momo Aluminium Sport gear
	knob which is basically like the Ferrari ones. Nareman says they
	are exceptionally good quality.
        <P>
        Nareman's friend also has a Tipo 16V and is looking for a written
        off Fiat Coupe 16V Turbo so that he can use the Turbo engine and
        gearbox in his Tipo. This should be an interesting project.
	<P>
	Towards the end of 1999 Nareman spent a fortune on repairing his
	Tipo. New clutch slave cylinder, new offside CV joint, new cambelt,
	new cambelt bearing, new cam-cover gasket, new exhaust, new hub-nuts,
	new gearbox oil, new power steering belt. In the summer of 1999
	he had a new gearbox, new brake master cylinder and replaced the
	sump gasket.
	<P>
	In July 1999 Nareman's gearbox broke, it didn't quite make it
	to 90,000 miles.
	 

